			"Message": "refactor(desktop): Simplify advanced synchronization service architecture\n\nThis commit significantly refactors the AdvancedSyncService to streamline the synchronization logic and reduce complexity. The changes focus on consolidating the synchronization flow and removing unnecessary abstractions.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Removed singleton pattern implementation in favor of direct instance export\n- Consolidated multiple interval-based synchronization methods into unified document and UI state synchronization\n- Simplified state management by removing complex nested UI state structures\n- Replaced separate performance monitoring and collaboration session handling with focused synchronization logic\n- Enhanced error handling with more granular error reporting and conflict resolution\n- Added manual sync triggering capability and improved service disposal\n\nThe refactoring maintains the core synchronization functionality while making the codebase more maintainable and easier to reason about. The service now handles document synchronization more efficiently with better conflict detection and resolution workflows.",
			"SHA": "bb4c8b03fac851939e31c91a1a220ce75db074c2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T06:19:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				353,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(desktop): Implement advanced synchronization service for Mountain integration\n\nThis commit introduces a comprehensive advanced synchronization service that enables real-time document synchronization and UI state management between the Wind frontend and Mountain backend. The service is designed to handle complex synchronization scenarios with support for conflict resolution, performance monitoring, and offline capabilities.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added detailed interfaces for document sync state, changes, UI state, and configuration\n- Implemented the AdvancedSyncService class with initialization, event listeners, and synchronization logic\n- Established connection to Mountain backend using Tauri APIs\n- Set up periodic synchronization with configurable intervals\n- Added error handling and event emission for sync status\n\nThe service integrates seamlessly with Mountain's WindAdvancedSync capabilities, providing a foundation for collaborative editing and multi-window UI consistency. Future work includes implementing advanced conflict resolution and offline synchronization as noted in the TODOs.",
			"SHA": "deb6c08c3842c1ce0930e72fe5abbbb7f61156bc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T06:08:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				353,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(auth): Correct handling of special characters in usernames\n\nCorrected a persistent login failure affecting users whose usernames contained special characters (e.g., '&', '#', '?'). The root cause was traced back to improper URL encoding of the username string on the backend before it was used in the database lookup query.\n\nThis commit implements proper encoding using the standard library function, ensuring special characters are handled correctly during the authentication sequence.",
			"SHA": "6bb969a05da94a69ff86bef5167b6ac03b6d6c21"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T05:56:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
